{"id": "reasoning-d0eed063-9299-55b5-8c24-03c0ab2a7ebd-0", "sessionId": "422bf0c3-019e-a3c2-0b19-09a4a66b19c5", "turnId": "turn-f62365e4f8dcef9678ebef32a78d524e", "createdAt": 1792348487984, "updatedAt": 1792348487984, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "reasoning", "text": "Now I see the production code. The residual is `F_external - F_int` (reduced). The Newton linearization: dR = K_ext_total·du... Actually R(u(q), lam) = F_ext(u) - F_int(u). dR/dq = (K_ext - K_T) reduced = K_red (as computed: reduce_tangent(u, K_T, F_int - F_external, K_ext_total) — presumably gives reduced d(F_ext - F_int)/dq, i.e., the tangent of the residual, which includes -K_T + K_ext plus geometric terms). dR/dlam = F_prop_red.\n\nNewton: K_red·dq + F_prop_red·dlam = -R? No wait. We want R_new = 0: R + dR = 0 → K_red dq + F_prop_red dlam = -R.\n\nBut the code solves: [K_red, -F_prop_red; row, 0] [dq; dlam] = [residual; constraint], i.e., K_red dq - F_prop_red dlam = residual = R.\n\nThat's wrong on two counts unless... hmm. Wait, maybe reduce_tangent returns the tangent of the INTERNAL force minus external, i.e., d(F_int - F_ext)/dq = -dR/dq. Then Newton for R=0: dR/dq dq + dR/dlam dlam = -R → -(K_red)·dq + F_prop_red dlam = -R → K_red dq - F_prop_red dlam = R. That matches the code! So the sign convention depends on what reduce_tangent returns.\n\nLet me check reduce_tangent in corotational.py. The probe passed `F_int - lam*F_prop` as the third arg, same as production (F_int - F_external). So the probe replicates production. And production fails at step 11 with maximum_iterations_reached, and the probe shows the residual exploding after the first update. So either reduce_tangent's convention is inconsistent with reduce_force's residual sign, or something else.\n\nLet me read reduce_tangent and reduce_force in corotational.py.", "summary": []}
