pect monotone convergence or at least residual reduction. The first update from a nearly-exact equilibrium state producing residual 4e5 (50× the load magnitude!) means the state moved VERY far — like uz moved way beyond, or some rotation DOF exploded.\n\nLet me compute: what dq satisfies K_red dq = F_prop_red·dlam with dlam=1.56? If the structure's stiffness in the control direction... the previous steps had dlam≈0.04 for duz=0.0167. For the same duz=0.0167, getting dlam=1.56 means the solve thinks the required load for that displacement is 40× higher — i.e., the tangent says the structure is 40× STIFFER... no wait, softer? dlam per duz larger means... hmm, actually in DC, the constraint fixes duz; the equilibrium rows determine the rest. dlam=1.56 means the load must increase a lot for that small displacement — the tangent indicates the structure suddenly stiffened 40×?? That contradicts the softening trend. OR the solve is garbage due to ill-conditioning.\n\nAlternatively the dq has huge components in a near-null direction of K_red that row_jac barely sees. Near-null direction of K_red = near-mechanism. The rotating MPC map with plasticity... \n\nI think the most informative next step: extend the probe to print the actual delta magnitudes, ||dq||, the condition/solve quality, and the residual predicted by the linearization vs actual. But the user said \"No broad investigation; run existing step11 discriminating probe first through harness. Then GENERAL augmented matrix correction and bounded rotating contactfree DC subdivision if needed.\"\n\nThe probe already discriminates: with GENERAL, the very first Newton update from an equilibrated state explodes the residual. So the matrix class is NOT the cause (probe already used GENERAL). The supervisor anticipated this: \"This is a compatible algebraic correction, but do not assert it causes the observed stall unless the recorded probe discriminates. The manual probe already uses GENERAL. Verify actual backend if releva