{"id": "reasoning-843a737b-a0c4-50e7-bebe-b3a3dc48a106-0", "sessionId": "422bf0c3-019e-a3c2-0b19-09a4a66b19c5", "turnId": "turn-f62365e4f8dcef9678ebef32a78d524e", "createdAt": 1792348523064, "updatedAt": 1792348523064, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "reasoning", "text": "Now I understand the structure. The step loop: `for local_step_index in range(1, num_steps+1)`, target = initial_control + target_increment * local_step_index / num_steps. On failure: restore q/lam, break (with failure_reason). \n\nThe adopted subdivision: on a failed control interval, discard trial, restore state exactly, subdivide only that control interval, retry within existing min-step control and task budget. Preserve every original scheduled control milestone. Record attempts/cutbacks/stop reason.\n\nDesign: within the step loop, wrap the Newton attempt in a retry loop over subdivisions of the current interval [prev_target, target]. On maximum_iterations_reached (or nonfinite/singular?), restore q/lam/states and retry with the interval split (e.g., halve), until the sub-increment falls below a min-step threshold. What is the \"existing min-step control\"? Let me check if there's a min step in DisplacementControl or NonlinearConvergenceSettings. Let me check the DisplacementControl dataclass (line ~371-400) and settings.\n\nAlso need to scope: \"bounded rotating contactfree DC subdivision\" — only for the rotating-MPC route (rotating_mpc_map is not None) and contact-free (contact_manager is None / augmented is None). Keep contact/moving-tool and legacy routes unchanged.\n\nLet me read the DisplacementControl class and check for min-step settings.", "summary": []}
