{"id": "reasoning-b58ad51f-0fb2-5693-a4a3-dd396d0929c6-0", "sessionId": "422bf0c3-019e-a3c2-0b19-09a4a66b19c5", "turnId": "turn-f62365e4f8dcef9678ebef32a78d524e", "createdAt": 1792348527444, "updatedAt": 1792348527444, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "reasoning", "text": "The DC solve function `_solve_static_displacement_control` doesn't currently take convergence settings — it's a plain fixed-increment loop. The adopted subdivision: \"on failed attempt discard trial, restore q/lam/history/contact state exactly, subdivide only that control interval, retry within the existing min-step control and task budget.\"\n\n\"existing min-step control\" — the force-control route has min_step_fraction in NonlinearConvergenceSettings. For DC there is no existing min-step. I'll implement a bounded subdivision: on iteration failure (maximum_iterations_reached) for the rotating contact-free route, restore state and halve the remaining interval, with a bounded number of cutbacks (e.g., min sub-increment = target_increment/num_steps / 2^max_cutbacks with max_cutbacks like 8, or a min-step fraction of the scheduled increment like 1/256). Record attempts/cutbacks in info and step records.\n\nDesign details:\n\n- Scope: only when `rotating_mpc_map is not None` and `contact_manager is None` (contact-free; augmented_contact_manager is None and not moving_tool). Legacy and contact routes unchanged.\n- Preserve every original scheduled milestone: the outer loop still iterates local_step_index 1..num_steps with the same targets. Within a step, if the Newton attempt fails with maximum_iterations_reached (also singular/nonfinite?), restore exactly and retry on subdivided intervals: sub-target = prev_target + (target - prev_target) * k/subdivisions. On success of all sub-intervals, the milestone target is reached (last sub-target = target exactly).\n- Bounded: sub-increment must stay >= min fraction of the scheduled increment, e.g., 1/2^8 = 1/256 of the original per-step increment; beyond that, fail with the original failure_reason and record stop reason like \"min_control_step_reached\".\n- Record: info[\"displacement_control_subdivisions\"] = {attempts, cutbacks, ...}; each accepted step record can include subdivisions used. Need to check the step record structure (NonlinearStaticStep) — adding new fields might break contracts. Let me check what step records contain and where they're appended after a successful step (the code after the failure handling, ~line 4180-4340).\n\nAlso the GENERAL correction: make the augmented factorization GENERAL unconditionally at both DC sites. \"both DC sites if applicable\" — there's the rotating-map site and the legacy site in this same function (the `aug = sparse.bmat(...)` block handles both via K_red etc.). The factorize call currently uses GENERAL if general_tangent else SYMMETRIC_INDEFINITE. Change to GENERAL unconditionally. Are there other DC sites? grep for other bmat/factorize with control rows — there's the moving-tool/contact route maybe in general_contact. The supervisor said \"Adopt MatrixClass.GENERAL for it unconditionally (both DC sites if applicable)\". Let me search for other augmented DC factorizations.\n\nAlso, the wrench test fix. Let me look at the failing wrench test in the continuation test file. And check what \"both DC sites\" might be — maybe there's another one in nonlinear_performance.py or elsewhere. Let me grep.", "summary": []}
