{"id": "reasoning-0a8d2a13-2cd2-5958-95d4-6a96a13e6974-0", "sessionId": "422bf0c3-019e-a3c2-0b19-09a4a66b19c5", "turnId": "turn-f62365e4f8dcef9678ebef32a78d524e", "createdAt": 1792349272016, "updatedAt": 1792349272016, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "reasoning", "text": "Interp: same signature. Terminal at uz -0.11354 (milestone 7 = -0.1167? wait: -0.11354166666666668... milestones: -0.0167·k. -0.11354 = -0.10 - 0.01354? Hmm: accepted_increments 10, lam 11.95. The interp milestones: -0.0167, -0.0333, ..., -0.10 (step 6), -0.1167 (step 7)... terminal ctrl -0.11354 = -0.10 - 0.01354? Actually -0.11354166666 = -0.10 - 0.013541666 = -0.10 - 0.0167·0.8125? Hmm, 0.0135416667/0.0166667 = 0.8125 = 13/16. So it's a subdivision target: -0.10 + (-0.0167)·(13/16)? That means milestone 7 (-0.1167) was attempted, cut back... and an increment at 13/16 of the interval was accepted? Wait, my scheme: fractions are 1/2^k of the REMAINING interval. From -0.10 toward -0.1167: 1/2 → -0.10833; if that failed, 1/4 → -0.10417... but accepted at -0.11354 = -0.10 - 0.0167·0.8125. 0.8125 = 0.5 + 0.25 + 0.0625 = 1/2 + 1/4 + 1/16. So successive accepted sub-intervals: half, then quarter of remainder, then... -0.10833 (1/2), then remaining [-0.10833, -0.1167]: 1/2 → -0.1125, then remaining [-0.1125, -0.1167]: 1/2 → -0.11458? Hmm -0.11354: -0.1125 + (-0.1167+0.1125)/2 = -0.11458 no. Let me not overanalyze: -0.11354166666 = -0.10 - 0.01354166666; 0.01354166666·48 = 0.65 = 0.0166667·0.8125. Eh. The exact composition doesn't matter.\n\nSame signature: FD consistent (error ~2.0, i.e., fd = -K_red; slightly off from 2.0 — 1.94-1.999 — due to FD noise at this state), K_red healthy, augmented σ_min 0.0062 (condition ~1.4e12) — same fold obstruction. Interp crossed beyond -0.10 (previously stalled at -0.083) — the subdivision helped interp too (it got to -0.11354, past the original -0.0833 stall and past -0.10), but the fold blocks it before -0.1167.\n\nSo both couplings: